I suggest we add the possibility for the shops (churches, towers, etc.)
to be multi-level. This would add variety to the game, without (I believe)
too much added complexity to the code.
(I think we need more variety. Not just new objects and similar _small_
additions, but something more radical, like multi-level shops.)

A multi-level shop has a base-level that is a traditional shop. The shop
keeper guards the door as usual. In addition there is an upwards going
staircase to the second level of the shop, etc. Although there are many
levels in the shop, there are only ONE SHOPKEEPER. 

The second (third, fourth) level is not an ordinary level. This level is
empty, save for the shop. The walls are non-diggable. If the base level
of the shop is on level 5, the additional levels are 5.1 , 5.2 , etc.
Although you can teleport out of level 5.2, you cannot teleport into 5.2.
When you use normal staircases, you go from level 4 to 5 to 6, thus not
noticing the multi-level shop.

You could implement the already suggested shopping mall this way if you
put different items on different levels.

Food stores could have cellars for vegetables, etc.

Towers on the castle level could have many levels.
